mindyourhead-by-macslow for Debian
---------------------------------

The upstream archive (mind-your-head-compo.tar.xz from scene.org,
Revision 2019 PC 4k intro compo) only contains a prebuilt x86-64 executable.
mind-your-head_by_MacSlow-fullscreen-1920x1080 has been unpacked and is
installed as is in /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/mindyourhead-by-macslow/.

The executable only links to libc and libdl: SDL 2 and OpenGL are opened at
run time with dlopen("libSDL2-2.0.so") and dlopen("libGL.so"). These
unversioned names are only shipped by the -dev packages, so
debian/mindyourhead-by-macslow.links creates them in the executable directory
(pointing to libSDL2-2.0.so.0 and libGL.so.1) and the launcher runs the intro
with LD_LIBRARY_PATH=./ .

executable seems to be compiled for an unknown distribution (no GCC version
string, crinkled 4k executable without section headers; upstream says it was
tested on Ubuntu 16.04 and 18.10)

